docs/agents/testing.md:109:| `404` on `->set()`/`->call()`, mutations don't persist (~75 failures) | Livewire endpoint hash mismatch (stale `routes-v7.php`) | `config:clear && route:clear` |
docs/agents/testing.md:119:| A tracked env file must never carry a real `APP_KEY` (#953) | `.env.example`, `.env.example.mysql`, `.env.example.pgsql`, `.env-example-github`, `.env.testing` and `.env.e2e.example` all ship `APP_KEY=` **blank**; `php artisan key:generate` produces the value per clone. `scripts/check-app-key-leak.php` fails the build on a non-empty one and runs from **both** `scripts/verify.sh` and the `lint` job in CI (the issue's step 3 said "fail the job" — `verify.sh` alone never runs in CI, whose jobs are `lint`/`test`/`coverage-report`/`typecheck`/`e2e`/`mutation`/`phpstan`/`test-php86`). Two rules make the guard usable: it reports **tracked files only** (your working `.env` is gitignored and MUST have a key), and it **never prints the value** (a CI log that echoes the secret republishes it). It reads the **git index**, not the working tree, so a per-clone key generated locally is not a finding. **`.env.testing` is tracked AND load-bearing**: `LoadEnvironmentVariables` swaps the env file to it when `APP_ENV=testing` and dotenv is immutable, so a blank key there beats a good `.env` key and kills >1000 tests with `MissingAppKeyException`. That is why `composer test` starts with `php scripts/ensure-test-app-key.php`, which generates one **only when there is none** — an unconditional `key:generate` would rewrite the tracked file on every run and put a fresh key one `git add` from a commit. Pinned by `AppKeyLeakGuardTest`, `AppKeyGuardWiringTest` and `TestAppKeyBootstrapTest` |
docs/agents/testing.md:135:## CI jobs (`.github/workflows/test.yml` — eight jobs, three blocking; `mutation` is manual-only)
docs/agents/testing.md:145:| `mutation` | Mutation Testing (`--covered-only`) | `continue-on-error`; manual-only (`workflow_dispatch`, #1012) |
docs/agents/testing.md:148:`mutation` is gated to `workflow_dispatch` (#1012): the job is green, but each run is expensive (checkout, composer install, `npm ci`, a Vite build and migrations before the single `pest --mutate` line) and it used to spend ~23 minutes on every PR on a signal that `continue-on-error` never gates. Re-enable on PRs by dropping the job's `if:`. A manual run executes every job, so read that job's own result rather than the run's conclusion — and note that the `workflow_dispatch` button appears only once this trigger is on the default branch (`main`).
docs/agents/testing.md:152:> yq -r '.jobs | keys | join(", ")' .github/workflows/test.yml              # lint, test, coverage-report, typecheck, e2e, mutation, phpstan, test-php86
AGENTS.md:134:`.github/workflows/test.yml` runs on PRs with **seven** jobs — three blocking (`lint` Pint, `test` Pest + coverage ≥80%, `phpstan`) and four `continue-on-error` (`coverage-report`, `typecheck`, `e2e`, `test-php86`); an eighth job, `mutation`, is manual-only behind `workflow_dispatch` (#1012). The job table + the yq derivation commands: [testing](docs/agents/testing.md). Coverage is CI-only.
--- features 180-190 ---
| `GenerateDailyReportsJob` | 600s | 2 | Runs `GenerateDailyReports` artisan command — **not dispatched by anything** (see the gotcha below); the 06:00 schedule runs the command inline (#1021) |
| `SyncZabbixJob` | 30s | 2 | Fetches Zabbix interface traffic, caches it as `zabbix_traffic_data` (5 min TTL); records a `zabbix_sync_logs` row per run (#740) |
| `SendNotificationJob` | 30s | 3 | Queued wrapper for one in-app notification, **per recipient**; dispatched only from `TicketCommentController` (comment create/update/delete). Not unit-scoped |

The two retention jobs accept a `$unitIds` array; **empty resolves `AccessService::allUnitIds()` (org-wide), NOT `accessibleUnitIds()`** (#836). `accessibleUnitIds()` reads `auth()`/`session()` and is therefore always `[]` in a scheduler or queue worker — every caller used to read that as "nothing to do" and exit successfully. `accessibleUnitIds()` is request-scoped UI code only. `GenerateDailyReportsJob` takes no scope of its own: it shells out to `reports:generate-daily`, which resolves the unit set itself. Those jobs have `failed()` methods that `Log::error()`. `SyncZabbixJob` takes no unit scope and records a **failure row** when `services.zabbix.out_item_id` / `in_item_id` are not configured.

> Gotcha: `GenerateDailyReportsJob` has **no dispatch site on purpose**. Its `$timeout` is 600s while the default `redis` connection's `retry_after` is 90s, so a dispatched run can be re-reserved and executed twice — it writes rows. `config/queue.php` already defines `redis-reports` (`retry_after` 600) for it, but the documented worker (`install-guid.md`) only serves the default `redis` connection, so dispatching it there would silently stop generating daily reports. Pin the connection + worker (issue #1010) before wiring this job into `bootstrap/app.php` (#1021).

> Gotcha: `NotificationService::send()` is the **static** primitive — it creates the in-app notification row and invalidates the recipient's bell cache. `SendNotificationJob` is only the queued per-recipient wrapper around it and has **no static `send()` of its own** (its surface is `__construct` / `handle` / `failed`). `SyncZabbixJob::alertAdmins()` calls `NotificationService::send()` **directly and synchronously** — it does not dispatch the job. Read both before adding a second notification path.

